        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 舞会",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "舞会 — wǔhuì — \"dance party; ball\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "zhè shì wǒ dìyī cì cānjiā wǔhuì — This is the first time I've been to a dance."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 舞 (wǔ) — fourteen strokes: on top eight, a short stroke falling left, two bars with four short verticals through the lower one, and a long bar across; below, on the left the top of 多 duō, three strokes, and on the right three strokes. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "舞会 (wǔhuì) is built from 舞 (wǔ) 'to dance' and 会 'a gathering', both inherited from Middle Chinese, mjuX and hwajH (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'singing and dancing' and the second 'to meet'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
